      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2002-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring, \\[ \\begin{gathered} (2x+3)\\left[(x-4)+(x-6)\\right] \\\\ = (2x+3)(2x-10) \\\\ = 0. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThe roots are \\(-\\dfrac{3}{2}\\) and \\(5,\\) which sum to \\(\\dfrac{7}{2}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
